# test/performance/profiles/ is NOT ignored. It was, back when it was scratch
# output. It now holds the measured data of record: the stored result JSON, the
# machine specifications captured on each target, the generated comparison
# documents, and analysis.md — including the R640 baseline, whose machine is
# offline and whose numbers exist nowhere else.

